+# 0001 — Scheduled plan changes live on the subscription
+
+Date: 2026-10-29 · Status: accepted
+
+## Context
+
+Downgrades and interval switches don't take effect until the period ends (see
+`specs/plan-changes.md`). Something has to remember them until the renewal happens. The
+production store is database-backed and has the same methods as `InMemoryStore`.
+
+## Decision
+
+`Subscription` gains two optional fields, `pending_plan_code: str | None` and
+`pending_interval: Interval | None`. They are either both set or both `None`. A subscription
+holds at most one scheduled change, and each plan change request replaces it. The
+renewal applies the scheduled change and then clears it.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The production store needs two nullable columns on subscriptions.
+- There is no history of scheduled changes that were replaced. Later work that needs
+  history, or more than one future change, has to move this into its own record.
